# Priority 5: End-to-End Composition Test — Phosphorus

## 1. Domain choice: phosphorus over groundwater

**Recommendation: phosphorus.**

| Criterion | Phosphorus | Groundwater |
|---|---|---|
| Moiety accounting | One conserved material; exact conservation proved (Article 013 Thm) | Anomaly-based; no absolute stock; no clean moiety |
| Module decomposition | Six compartments with explicit donor-limited fluxes | Multiple basins; recharge mechanisms uncharacterized |
| Barrier conditions | Donor-limited tangency gives clean barrier margins | Requires hydraulic conductivity, storage geometry |
| Cross-scale structure | Geological → active → living → product → sink | Basin → aquifer → well; trade/catchment structure present but less typed |
| Data grounding | Reserve-life ratio (~309 yr); USGS reserves | G3P anomaly trends; partial empirical grounding |
| Composition exercise | Natural 3–5 module decomposition with directed coupling | Better suited for epistemic/institutional layers (second test) |

Phosphorus exercises the **typed accounting, conservation, invariance, and composition** layers of the architecture. Groundwater is better reserved for a second test that exercises the **epistemic, partial-observation, and governance-delay** layers.

