## 11. Recommended next steps

1. **Numerical instantiation:** Choose a specific phosphorus system (e.g., a catchment or national phosphorus budget) and compute the small-gain margins numerically. This requires data on $\mu, K_A, m, h, d_U, e_{GA}, e_{AG}, c_G, r_P, \rho$.

2. **Groundwater epistemic test:** Use the G3P anomaly data and the governance-delay framework from Article 011 to exercise the epistemic/institutional layers. This would be the second end-to-end test, complementary to phosphorus.

3. **Strategic composition module:** Extend the composition theorem to include strategic modules (e.g., mining companies choosing $c_G$ non-cooperatively). This would exercise the strategic contract modality from the master manuscript.

4. **Commons governance module:** Instantiate the commons-allocation template (Appendix F of the master manuscript) for the phosphorus sink $W$. This would require an allocation rule for retirement losses across product categories.

